## Smallest proposed host change — not yet authorized

A fresh disposable standard Ubuntu runner could reclaim space from its
preinstalled Android SDK at the exact root `/usr/local/lib/android/sdk`.
That SDK root is documented in the official
[Ubuntu 24.04 image inventory](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/actions/runner-images/main/images/ubuntu/Ubuntu2404-Readme.md).
Its actual existence, identity, symlink/mount boundaries and reclaimable size on
the new VM must be checked before any deletion. No particular reclaimable byte
count is assumed from the inventory.

The proposal is limited to that unused SDK on the new GitHub VM, followed by one
fresh capacity/setup check. It must not delete or modify the Mac, checkout,
model/data, `/opt/hostedtoolcache`, Python, Docker storage, general caches or other
SDK roots. It must not install packages, acquire the software image, run the full
native pipeline, retry the consumed attempt, start a GPU, or train.

Deletion would not be recoverable within that VM without reinstalling the SDK;
the next standard GitHub job starts from a fresh provider image. This proposed
deletion and fresh workflow require explicit approval before implementation and
publication. If its checks cannot establish the exact target or adequate space,
stop rather than expanding deletion targets or lowering the floor.

An alternative is a separately approved dedicated CPU host with adequate disk,
which introduces new host, provisioning and cost decisions. Neither alternative
has been executed. A successful capacity check would still not prove Docker,
cgroup or full worker qualification, nor explain the old host retroactively.

Gate 5 remains incomplete. This turn made only read-only repository/API/docs
checks and this local status note; no commit, push, workflow, instance, cleanup,
acquisition or training action occurred.
